      <td style="padding-top:0in;padding-left:0in;vertical-align:top;padding-bottom:0in;padding-right:0in;"><p style="font-size:9pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">We have not made any material changes in the accounting methodology used to calculate our write-down and shrinkage reserves in the past three fiscal years. We do not believe there is a reasonable likelihood that there will be a material change in the future estimates we use to calculate our inventory reserves. However, if actual results are not consistent with our estimates, we may be exposed to losses or gains that could be material.</span><span style="color:#ff0000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> </span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Our inventory reserves were $3.7 million at January 31, 2026 compared to $3.2 million at February 1, 2025, representing an increase of $0.5  in fiscal 2025.</span></p><p style="font-size:9pt;margin-top:12pt;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">A 10% decrease in the sales price of our inventory at January 31, 2026 would have decreased net income by $0.6 million in fiscal 2025.</span></p><p style="font-size:9pt;margin-top:12pt;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">A 10% increase in actual physical inventory shrinkage rate at January 31, 2026 would have decreased net income by less than $0.1 million in fiscal 2025.</span></p></td>
